  "notes": "USAGE:\n{防止|ぼうし} is almost always used as a compound modifier ({防止|ぼうし} + noun) or with する. It sounds formal and is common in official contexts, signage, and policy language.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {事故|じこ}{防止|ぼうし} (accident prevention)\n- {犯罪|はんざい}{防止|ぼうし} (crime prevention)\n- {再発|さいはつ}{防止|ぼうし} (prevention of recurrence)\n- {感染|かんせん}{防止|ぼうし} (infection prevention)\n- {防止|ぼうし}{策|さく} (preventive measure)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {防止|ぼうし}: prevention (stopping something before it happens; formal, policy-oriented)\n- {予防|よぼう}: prevention (proactive measures, especially medical; {予防|よぼう}{接種|せっしゅ} = vaccination)\n- {阻止|そし}: blocking, thwarting (stopping something already in motion)",
